---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ChangelogGenerator from '../../components/ChangelogGenerator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="AI Changelog Generator"
  description="Turn a list of commit messages into a clean, user-facing changelog entry — bring your own Anthropic API key."
>
  <ChangelogGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>From commit log to release notes</h2>
  <p>
    Raw commit messages are written for developers, not end users — they're
    often too technical or too terse for a public changelog. This tool
    converts a batch of commits into a grouped, plain-language changelog
    entry your users can actually understand.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Enter your API key (stored only in your browser).</li>
    <li>Paste your commit messages since the last release, one per line.</li>
    <li>Set the version number and generate.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Does it filter out internal-only commits?</strong> It does its
    best to focus on user-facing changes based on the wording, but review
    the output — you may want to remove entries that are purely internal
    (like refactors with no user impact).
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
